From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/matroskadec: start a seek at the earliest key frame
 of the video tracks

matroska_read_seek() takes the position of the cluster to start at from the
index of the one stream the caller seeks on (the default stream, for
av_seek_frame() with a stream index of -1). A file with two video tracks
that are one picture, such as the base and the enhancement layer of Dolby
Vision profile 7 in two tracks, or the two views of a 3D file, has a key
frame in each track at the same time, and the muxer may put the cluster of
one of them before the cluster of the other. Seeking on the track whose
cluster is the later one starts after the key frame of the other track:
the demuxer then delivers that track from its next key frame on, up to a
whole GOP later, and the pictures in between have no enhancement layer.

Start at the earliest cluster that holds a key frame of a video track at
the time of the one found: for each other video track that is not an
attached picture, the index entry at exactly that time (in that track's
time base), if it has one and it is at an earlier position. As after any
seek, the packets of an earlier time (subtitles apart) are dropped until a
key frame at or after that time is read, and the track sought on starts at
its own key frame; the other video track now starts at its key frame too.
A track with no entry at that time does not change anything: a file
whose tracks have key frames at other times, or whose cues name one track
only (until the demuxer has read that part of the file: it indexes every
key frame it reads). No file with a single video track changes.

Tested with libavformat built from this tree, 122 seeks to 1.5 s after each
key frame of two 4K+1080p Dolby Vision profile 7 files of 122 key frames in
each track, the same pictures, the clusters of the enhancement layer first
in one and last in the other: before, the enhancement layer starts on a
non-key frame after 122 of 122 seeks in the first and 0 of 122 in the
second; after, 0 and 0. In a third file whose layers have key frames at
other times (7 of the 120 of the base layer have an enhancement key frame
at that time, in the cluster before in 6) the 6 now start with it. Ten
files with one video track each (two of them one-track Dolby Vision, one
H.264 MVC, one with 87 streams, two with two editions, one with subtitles)
give the same packets after 60 seeks each, backward and forward, before and
after.
---
 libavformat/matroskadec.c | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/matroskadec.c b/libavformat/matroskadec.c
index 235f35b..d996aa6 100644
--- a/libavformat/matroskadec.c
+++ b/libavformat/matroskadec.c
@@ -4635,6 +4635,7 @@ static int matroska_read_seek(AVFormatContext *s, int stream_index,
     MatroskaTrack *tracks = NULL;
     AVStream *st = s->streams[stream_index];
     FFStream *const sti = ffstream(st);
+    int64_t pos;
     int i, index;
 
     /* Parse the CUES now since we need the index data to seek. */
@@ -4671,8 +4672,32 @@ static int matroska_read_seek(AVFormatContext *s, int stream_index,
         tracks[i].end_timecode         = 0;
     }
 
+    /* The key frame is in the cluster the index of this stream names, but the key frame of
+     * another video track at the same time (the enhancement layer of a Dolby Vision file
+     * with two tracks, the second view of a 3D one) may be in an earlier cluster. Start at
+     * the earliest of them, as every video track needs its own key frame to start from;
+     * the packets of the clusters in between that are before the key frame are dropped,
+     * as they are after any seek. */
+    pos = sti->index_entries[index].pos;
+    for (i = 0; i < s->nb_streams; i++) {
+        AVStream *other = s->streams[i];
+        FFStream *const osti = ffstream(other);
+        int64_t ts;
+        int j;
+
+        if (other == st || other->codecpar->codec_type != AVMEDIA_TYPE_VIDEO ||
+            (other->disposition & AV_DISPOSITION_ATTACHED_PIC) || !osti->nb_index_entries)
+            continue;
+        ts = av_rescale_q(sti->index_entries[index].timestamp, st->time_base,
+                          other->time_base);
+        j = av_index_search_timestamp(other, ts, AVSEEK_FLAG_BACKWARD);
+        if (j >= 0 && osti->index_entries[j].timestamp == ts &&
+            osti->index_entries[j].pos < pos)
+            pos = osti->index_entries[j].pos;
+    }
+
     /* We seek to a level 1 element, so set the appropriate status. */
-    matroska_reset_status(matroska, 0, sti->index_entries[index].pos);
+    matroska_reset_status(matroska, 0, pos);
     if (flags & AVSEEK_FLAG_ANY) {
         sti->skip_to_keyframe = 0;
         matroska->skip_to_timecode = timestamp;
